 disease</article-title><source>J Card Surg</source><year>2005</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>160</fpage><lpage>3</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15725141</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R15"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kobayashi</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Sakata</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Kinjo</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Yotsumoto</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Matsumoto</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Iguro</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Off-pump coronary artery bypass grafting in a patient with Behcet&#x02019;s disease</article-title><source>Jpn J Thorac Cardiovasc Surg</source><year>2004</year><volume>52</volume><fpage>527</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15609645</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-wrap><fig id="F1" position="float"><label>Fig. (1)</label><caption><p>Coronary angiography revealed an aneurysm of the right coronary artery with tight stenosis of the posterolateral branch.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="TOCMJ-2-118_F1"/></fig><fig id="F2" position="float"><label>Fig. (2)</label><caption><p>Coronary angiography showed total occlusion of the right coronary.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="TOCMJ-2-118_F2"/></fig></floats-wrap></article>